A||N||6||MikeSchaefer||I'm losing faith in these cars..... engine trouble is killing me||||8||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||04-23-2001||12:43 AM||||I bought an 84 with that had undergone a ground-up restoration and got an 87 V-6, seems to be an all-around great car, but it is starting to get on my nerves.  When I bought it, it had virtually no sensors on it, the guy had it rigged up for racing or something, so I took it to Fiero Bob and put in about $750 worth of sensors.  I then started to notice that when I stepped on the gas every once in a while it would kind of putter and not go right away.  Then a few months later the transmission went out, it needed a new transmission and knock-on valve, I had Fiero Bob do that and it ran me another $1000 or so.  Just about a month ago the reoccurring problem of sputtering at stop signs had grown into a major problem.  So I took it to Bob about 3 weeks ago, he did all sorts of work to it and only charged me $400, because he's the nicest mechanic in the world.  It ran perfectly on Friday when I got it back, like a new car, then today I took it out, and every simptom that I had on it before I got it fixed last time had returned.  Except now it is so bad that the car won't go over 5 mph, it just sputters.....  AHHHH, I thought I was the most dedicated Fiero lover ever, but now I'm questioning if it is all worth it.  I can hardly ever even drive my car, and I can barely afford to keep it running.......<BR>oh well,<BR>Mike  <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> <BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||sjp777||04-23-2001||12:46 AM||||Check to see if the element in your cat has melted down and is blocking the exhaust. Easy and cheap to fix.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||04-23-2001||12:51 AM||||that was the first thing that I checked when the troubles first started.  I guess most of the symptoms on my car are about the same as those of a blocked cat, but unfortunately it wasn't that.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||04-23-2001||02:54 AM||||Mike, is yours an automatic or a stick?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MikeSchaefer||04-23-2001||02:55 AM||||It's an Automatic, any ideas?<BR>Thanks a million,<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||04-23-2001||10:49 AM||||I know this might sound strange, but you said the car was an 84 and you have an 87 V-6. You also stated the guy by-passed sensors and that Bob corrected it. Just out of curiosity, was the Eprom changed? Is it a V-6/auto prom? Do you happen to know if it sputters worse when the weather is damp/humid? My first Fiero would "lose it's mind" occasionally when the air was damp or very humid. Turned out it was a bad harness connector to the engine. When moisture increased, the corrosion absorbed the moisture and caused all kinds of intermittent problems and false readings to the ECM. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||MikeSchaefer||04-27-2001||01:04 AM||||Whoa, I didn't notice your post Oreif, Yeah the eprom is out of the 87, What harness in particular was the culprit?  I don't think the weather is affecting mine, but I can check to see if there is corrosion or something.  It has gotten really bad now, the car won't even move without dying, the only way I can even keep it alive is to immediately press on the gas and keep it over 1200 rpms in park.  My parents have been trying to talk me into selling my car, that definately won't happen, but it is becoming the laughing stock of the town.  God I need a v8 or something.  <BR>Thanks again for the insight guys, I really appreciate it. <BR>Mike <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||3
